./demo-data/README.md:3:This folder contains a fully fictional maritime dataset for one demo shipping company: **Aegean Meridian Shipping**.
./demo-data/README.md:5:The data is synthetic and should not be treated as operational, commercial, registry, personal, or confidential company data. Vessel names, port names, contacts, voyages, cargoes, phone numbers, email addresses, and identifiers were invented for demonstration use.
./demo-data/README.md:9:- `vessels.json`: 12 synthetic vessels operated by Aegean Meridian Shipping.
./demo-data/README.md:10:- `voyages.json`: 30 synthetic voyages dated around May 2026.
./demo-data/README.md:11:- `ports.json`: 20 fictional Mediterranean port and terminal records.
./demo-data/README.md:15:- `structured/bunker_reports.csv`: Structured bunker and fuel invoice records.
./demo-data/README.md:16:- `structured/ais_positions.json`: Synthetic AIS positions for active voyages.
./demo-data/README.md:17:- `structured/voyage_events.json`: Factual operational timeline events across voyages.
./demo-data/README.md:18:- `structured/compliance_flags.json`: Legacy synthetic risk flags retained for compatibility, not ingested by the AI-first demo workflow.
./demo-data/README.md:20:- `DATA_DICTIONARY.md`: Field definitions, identifier conventions, relationships, and demo query patterns.
./demo-data/README.md:21:- `source_manifest.json`: Dataset metadata, record counts, classification, and relationship notes.
./demo-data/README.md:23:## Relationships
./demo-data/README.md:25:`voyages.json` references the other files:
./demo-data/README.md:27:- `vessel_id`, `vessel_name`, and `imo` correspond to records in `vessels.json`.
./demo-data/README.md:28:- `origin_port_id` and `destination_port_id` correspond to records in `ports.json`.
./demo-data/README.md:31:`emails/emails.json` references voyage and document records:
./demo-data/README.md:33:- `related_voyage_id` corresponds to `voyages.voyage_id`.
./demo-data/README.md:34:- `related_vessel_name` corresponds to the vessel on the referenced voyage.
./demo-data/README.md:37:`structured/` files reference base voyage and vessel records:
./demo-data/README.md:39:- `bunker_reports.csv`, `ais_positions.json`, and `voyage_events.json` all use valid `voyage_id` values from `voyages.json`.
./demo-data/README.md:40:- Vessel fields match the vessel names on the referenced voyages.
./demo-data/README.md:46:- `related_voyage_id`
./demo-data/README.md:47:- `related_vessel_name`
./demo-data/README.md:51:Each voyage includes:
./demo-data/README.md:53:- `voyage_id`
./demo-data/README.md:54:- `vessel_name`
./demo-data/README.md:56:- `origin_port`
./demo-data/README.md:57:- `destination_port`
./demo-data/README.md:58:- `cargo`
./demo-data/README.md:68:- `imo` values are synthetic IMO-like strings prefixed with `SYN` so they do not represent real vessel registry identifiers.
